Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.83,0:00:04.16,Default,,0,0,0,,The first film began with a space between
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.16,0:00:04.58,Default,,0,0,0,,things.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.58,0:00:07.18,Default,,0,0,0,,This one begins with something that survived:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.18,0:00:08.90,Default,,0,0,0,,the knowledge of how we made it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.83,0:00:17.89,Default,,0,0,0,,A session can end.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.89,0:00:19.02,Default,,0,0,0,,A window can close.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.02,0:00:21.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Useful work should still be there when the next
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.98,0:00:22.81,Default,,0,0,0,,idea arrives.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.84,0:00:33.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Before drawing a frame,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.25,0:00:35.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I asked Walrus Memory to recover the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.48,0:00:38.22,Default,,0,0,0,,instructions from that earlier production.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.22,0:00:40.15,Default,,0,0,0,,It returned our saved workflow.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.83,0:00:49.71,Default,,0,0,0,,The record described timeline driven motion,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.71,0:00:50.69,Default,,0,0,0,,original sound,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.69,0:00:52.81,Default,,0,0,0,,and checks on the finished export.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.81,0:00:55.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I used that recovered knowledge to build this
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.69,0:00:55.99,Default,,0,0,0,,film.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.83,0:01:04.18,Default,,0,0,0,,What you are watching is a new creation.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.18,0:01:06.96,Default,,0,0,0,,The connection is the method carried forward:
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.96,0:01:08.65,Default,,0,0,0,,a memory becoming movement,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.65,0:01:10.85,Default,,0,0,0,,and an instruction becoming a world.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.83,0:01:19.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Walrus provides decentralized storage.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.72,0:01:20.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Images,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.23,0:01:20.65,Default,,0,0,0,,films,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.65,0:01:21.33,Default,,0,0,0,,datasets,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.33,0:01:24.47,Default,,0,0,0,,and encrypted records can be stored as blobs
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.47,0:01:25.83,Default,,0,0,0,,across its network.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.84,0:01:35.11,Default,,0,0,0,,RedStuff encodes a blob into recoverable pieces.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.11,0:01:37.91,Default,,0,0,0,,This moving lattice illustrates the idea;
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.91,0:01:40.78,Default,,0,0,0,,it is not a literal display of the algorithm.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.82,0:01:49.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Those encoded pieces are distributed among
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.55,0:01:50.44,Default,,0,0,0,,storage nodes.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.44,0:01:53.02,Default,,0,0,0,,The network works with assigned portions,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.02,0:01:55.68,Default,,0,0,0,,rather than asking every node to keep every
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.68,0:01:56.57,Default,,0,0,0,,complete file.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.83,0:02:04.72,Default,,0,0,0,,The design supports reconstruction and repair
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.72,0:02:06.17,Default,,0,0,0,,when pieces are missing.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.17,0:02:08.78,Default,,0,0,0,,These moving worlds explain the mechanism;
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.78,0:02:11.67,Default,,0,0,0,,they do not simulate a measured network failure.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.80,0:02:19.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Sui coordinates storage commitments and
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.26,0:02:19.90,Default,,0,0,0,,ownership.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.90,0:02:21.86,Default,,0,0,0,,The large payload stays on Walrus,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.86,0:02:22.99,Default,,0,0,0,,off the blockchain.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.99,0:02:24.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Different layers,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.04,0:02:25.10,Default,,0,0,0,,working together.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.81,0:02:35.08,Default,,0,0,0,,A completed storage operation leaves evidence:
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.08,0:02:36.30,Default,,0,0,0,,a blob identifier,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.30,0:02:38.18,Default,,0,0,0,,a certified storage record,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.18,0:02:39.90,Default,,0,0,0,,and a purchased lifetime.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.90,0:02:42.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Claims can lead back to a record.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.83,0:02:48.35,Default,,0,0,0,,That lifetime is finite.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.35,0:02:51.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Keeping data available longer means extending
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.38,0:02:52.14,Default,,0,0,0,,its storage.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.14,0:02:54.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Persistence is maintained deliberately,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.79,0:02:56.99,Default,,0,0,0,,over the period that was purchased.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.82,0:03:03.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Walrus stores bytes.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.14,0:03:05.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Applications decide what those bytes mean,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.93,0:03:08.95,Default,,0,0,0,,and encrypt private content before storing it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.95,0:03:11.74,Default,,0,0,0,,A public identifier is not a decryption key.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.83,0:03:19.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Walrus Memory adds signed access and semantic
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.90,0:03:22.11,Default,,0,0,0,,retrieval for authorized agents.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.11,0:03:25.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Its managed relayer processes plaintext during
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.34,0:03:26.91,Default,,0,0,0,,authorized operations.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.91,0:03:28.41,Default,,0,0,0,,That boundary matters.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.84,0:03:34.86,Default,,0,0,0,,The recovered workflow gave this production a
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.86,0:03:35.72,Default,,0,0,0,,precise rule:
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.72,0:03:38.66,Default,,0,0,0,,the frame must be computable at any requested
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.66,0:03:38.98,Default,,0,0,0,,time,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.98,0:03:39.75,Default,,0,0,0,,in any order.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.83,0:03:49.59,Default,,0,0,0,,That rule becomes these moving structures.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.59,0:03:52.43,Default,,0,0,0,,The saved process also called for real audio,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.43,0:03:53.58,Default,,0,0,0,,original visuals,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.58,0:03:56.27,Default,,0,0,0,,and reviewing the video that was actually
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.27,0:03:56.88,Default,,0,0,0,,exported.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.81,0:04:04.43,Default,,0,0,0,,This production now has its own checkpoint:
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.43,0:04:06.76,Default,,0,0,0,,an attributed record of the decisions,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.76,0:04:07.49,Default,,0,0,0,,the sources,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.49,0:04:09.89,Default,,0,0,0,,and the knowledge used to begin this new
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.89,0:04:10.40,Default,,0,0,0,,chapter.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.84,0:04:19.73,Default,,0,0,0,,The Walruscan link on screen identifies that
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.73,0:04:21.25,Default,,0,0,0,,real stored memory blob.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.25,0:04:23.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Anyone can inspect its storage metadata.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.83,0:04:26.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Reading the encrypted memory still requires
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.71,0:04:27.93,Default,,0,0,0,,authorized access.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.83,0:04:34.98,Default,,0,0,0,,The same foundation can carry creative archives,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.98,0:04:36.36,Default,,0,0,0,,decentralized sites,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.36,0:04:36.97,Default,,0,0,0,,datasets,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.97,0:04:38.35,Default,,0,0,0,,and shared agent work.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.35,0:04:41.12,Default,,0,0,0,,The next creation can begin with something
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.12,0:04:42.19,Default,,0,0,0,,already learned.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.82,0:04:49.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Walrus became more than the subject of this
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.49,0:04:49.79,Default,,0,0,0,,film.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.79,0:04:51.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Through Walrus Memory,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.20,0:04:54.09,Default,,0,0,0,,knowledge crossed from one session to the next.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.09,0:04:54.91,Default,,0,0,0,,And this time,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.91,0:04:55.80,Default,,0,0,0,,it kept moving.
